From c63287c649d3bd866f6fe9adc2e23f64f6b64e23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:26:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Name a Linux host in guest notices

The Linux launcher passes tryomarchy.host=linux. With it, the Try Omarchy
Settings launcher, file drop notices and the file transfer window speak of
the host computer instead of Windows. Without it, Windows wording is
unchanged. The Settings and file transfer desktop entries now use wording
that fits either host.

Compatibility revision 47 delivers the scripts to existing disks.
---
